# Data + artefacts – never committed. Datasets live on HF Hub, models on the CDN.
data/pool/

# `data/legacy/` is 138 MB of imported imagery and is not committed - with THREE
# exceptions, none of which is derived data. `adjudication.json` is the record of
# 403 human form-factor decisions: who decided what, and when. Nothing can
# regenerate it. The legacy labels are waste STREAMS and a stream does not
# determine a shape - measured, the stream-derived mapping is wrong on 28.8 % of
# these very crops. Losing it means a person looking at 403 pictures again.
#
# Git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so the
# directories are walked open and their contents excluded instead. Do not
# collapse this back to `data/legacy/`.
data/legacy/*
!data/legacy/pool/
data/legacy/pool/*
!data/legacy/pool/adjudication.json
# The other two are docs/12 P3's, and they are here for the same reason.
# `colour-labels.json` is 160 body-and-lid decisions with a `labeller` on every
# row - currently `claude`, marked `provisional_proposals`, awaiting the
# maintainer's spot-check. Dropping it would throw away the pass AND the record
# of who made it, which is the part that decides whether P3 may close.
# `colour-sample.json` is regenerable by construction - seed 20260821, and
# `sample` refuses to overwrite a different draw - but committing it is what
# makes "the sample was frozen before the labels" a fact a reader can check
# rather than a claim in a document.
!data/legacy/pool/colour-labels.json
!data/legacy/pool/colour-sample.json
artifacts/
runs/
*.pt
*.onnx
*.zip
!data/taxonomy/**

